# Read by Vite on `npm run build` only — `npm run dev` boots the fixture loop
# and never looks at this (spec-client §5.4).
#
# The ORIGIN only. `src/transport/wire.ts`'s `joinCallUrl()` appends the route
# itself, so a value ending in /dday/call produces /dday/call/dday/call. A
# trailing slash is stripped and harmless.
#
# Not a secret — it ships inside the bundle and is public the moment the game
# deploys (contract-calls §11). Re-read it from the stack after any redeploy
# that replaces the API:
#
#   aws cloudformation describe-stacks --profile nhn-game \
#     --region ap-northeast-2 --stack-name nhn-game-proxy \
#     --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey==`CallEndpoint`].OutputValue' \
#     --output text
#
# Unset is not an error: the transport degrades to its fixture provider and the
# desk still plays, which is what keeps a Pages deploy green while the stack is
# down.
VITE_PROXY_BASE_URL=https://bm86and5hb.execute-api.ap-northeast-2.amazonaws.com
